 question...\r\n\r\nI am able to successfully create a TPU VM and get jax working with TPU support. However after stopping the instance and starting it again (with no changes to the system) I cannot access the TPU anymore:\r\n\r\n```\r\n>>> import jax\r\n>>> jax.devices()\r\nWARNING:absl:No GPU/TPU found, falling back to CPU. (Set TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=0 and rerun for more info.)\r\n[CpuDevice(id=0)]\r\n>>> TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=0\r\n>>> jax.devices()\r\n[CpuDevice(id=0)]\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tried running `TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=0; python3` and it gives me some extra info:\r\n```\r\nTPU platform initialization failed: NOT_FOUND: No ba16c7433 device found.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere is a [stack overflow question that is similar](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/73117166/why-is-the-tpu-not-recognized-on-my-google-cloud-tpu-vm-instance#comment130266883_73117166). But so far no answer.\n\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\n\njax[tpu]==0.3.17, jaxlib==0.3.15\n\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\n\nv2.8 TPU\n\n### Additional System Info\n\nUsing tpu-vm-base","closed_at":"2022-09-20T02:04:59Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1332458?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisflesher","id":1332458,"login":"chrisflesher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzI0NTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisflesher/subscri